  "name": "orders__phone",
  "status": "missing",
  "verdict": "missing baseline — committed, but no capture this run: its test was removed, renamed or skipped, or failed before it captured (the report cannot say which; the test run's log can); nothing to approve (approving only promotes a new capture) — to accept an intended removal, delete its baseline directory (.testivai/baselines/orders__phone) in the same change",
  "baseline": {
    "directory": ".testivai/baselines/orders__phone",
    "files": [
      ".testivai/baselines/orders__phone/screenshot.png",
      ".testivai/baselines/orders__phone/dom.html",
      ".testivai/baselines/orders__phone/metadata.json",
      ".testivai/baselines/orders__phone/elements.json"
    ]
  },
  "guidance": [
    "No capture this run: the baseline is committed (.testivai/baselines/orders__phone), but the test run captured nothing under this name, so there is no current image and nothing to diff. The report cannot say why: the test may have been removed or renamed, skipped, or failed before it captured. Check what the change under test did to that test or snapshot, and the test run's log for a failed or skipped test.",
    "Approving does nothing here: approve_snapshot and `testivai approve` only promote a new capture from .testivai/temp, and there is none. To accept an intended removal, delete the baseline directory in the same change (git rm -r .testivai/baselines/orders__phone); otherwise restore the test, or what it needs to reach its capture.",
    "There is no capture to call bad, so this is not a glitch: an intended change if the change under test meant to remove or rename it, a bug if it did so by mistake or broke the test before its capture, otherwise a possible bug."
  ]
}

